{"name":"Lord Baltimore","hex":"#b76764","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lord","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The master of the servants of a household;  the master of a feudal manor","One possessing similar mastery over others;  any feudal superior generally; any nobleman or aristocrat; any chief, prince, or sovereign ruler; in Scotland, a male member of the lowest rank of nobility (the equivalent rank in England is baron)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To domineer or act like a lord.","To invest with the dignity, power, and privileges of a lord; to grant the title of lord."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lord"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baltimore (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Baltimore is an American horror comic book series created by Mike Mignola and Christopher Golden. The series originally began with an illustrated novel, Baltimore, or, The Steadfast Tin Soldier and the Vampire in 2007. It followed the story of Lord Baltimore's hunt of the vampire Haigus as told by his three friends, Doctor Lemuel Rose, Thomas Childress Jr., and Demetrius Aischros. The series is a part of Mignola and Golden's Outerverse, a shared universe with Joe Golem and other titles such as Lady Baltimore."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c4/Baltimore%2C_or%2C_The_Steadfast_Tin_Soldier_and_the_Vampire_%28Dark_Horse_paperback_edition%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baltimore_(comics)"},{"title":"Lord Baltimore (The Blacklist)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lord Baltimore\" is the first episode of the second season of the American crime drama The Blacklist. The episode premiered in the United States on NBC on September 22, 2014."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_Baltimore_(The_Blacklist)"},{"title":"Lord","blocks":[{"text":"Lord is an appellation for a person or deity who has authority, control, or power over others, acting as a master, chief, or ruler. The appellation can also denote certain persons who hold a title of the peerage in the United Kingdom, or are entitled to courtesy titles. The collective \"Lords\" can refer to a group or body of peers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c4/Baltimore%2C_or%2C_The_Steadfast_Tin_Soldier_and_the_Vampire_%28Dark_Horse_paperback_edition%29.jpg/250px-Baltimore%2C_or%2C_The_Steadfast_Tin_Soldier_and_the_Vampire_%28Dark_Horse_paperback_edition%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c4/Baltimore%2C_or%2C_The_Steadfast_Tin_Soldier_and_the_Vampire_%28Dark_Horse_paperback_edition%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c4/Baltimore%2C_or%2C_The_Steadfast_Tin_Soldier_and_the_Vampire_%28Dark_Horse_paperback_edition%29.jpg/250px-Baltimore%2C_or%2C_The_Steadfast_Tin_Soldier_and_the_Vampire_%28Dark_Horse_paperback_edition%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaltimore%2C_or%2C_The_Steadfast_Tin_Soldier_and_the_Vampire_(Dark_Horse_paperback_edition).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Beowulf_-_hlaford.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Beowulf_-_hlaford.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The Old English word 'hlaford' evolved into 'lord'.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeowulf_-_hlaford.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Charles_Pepys%2C_1st_Earl_of_Cottenham_by_Charles_Robert_Leslie_cropped.jpg/500px-Charles_Pepys%2C_1st_Earl_of_Cottenh